  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  *
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  * @param[in]  *S        points to an instance of the Q31 Biquad cascade structure.
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  * @param[in]  *pSrc     points to the block of input data.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  * @param[out] *pDst     points to the block of output data.
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  * @param[in]  blockSize number of samples to process per call.
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  * @return     none.
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  *
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  * \par
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  * This function is optimized for speed at the expense of fixed-point precision and overflow protec
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  * The result of each 1.31 x 1.31 multiplication is truncated to 2.30 format.
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  * These intermediate results are added to a 2.30 accumulator.
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  * Finally, the accumulator is saturated and converted to a 1.31 result.
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  * The fast version has the same overflow behavior as the standard version and provides less precis
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  * In order to avoid overflows completely the input signal must be scaled down by two bits and lie 
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  * arm_biquad_cascade_df1_init_q31() to initialize filter structure.
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  *
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  * \par
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  * Refer to the function <code>arm_biquad_cascade_df1_q31()</code> for a slower implementation of t
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  * Use the function <code>arm_biquad_cascade_df1_init_q31()</code> to initialize the filter structu
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_fast_q31.c ****  */
